 vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418279 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c34e270-4cf3-5d2a-b3fd-ef4bc7870b05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418260} {:answer/id #uuid "5be21875-0229-56c7-bb70-8c2f8cf5c248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418262} {:answer/id #uuid "729b3e7f-da36-57dd-a802-b42075c33425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418263} {:answer/id #uuid "e6adc930-80cb-509e-93e9-9dc627ba31be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418272} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a2e377-db56-5763-bfa4-c0f31db675b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418262} :answer-field/id #uuid "166c2a53-a365-54bc-93bb-986af1335833" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418275}] :question/id #uuid "042d970d-9326-52e7-be56-f67cc5dc1c6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-111295" :question/problem "Given that  $\\text{Null}(A)={\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}$, find a basis for $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\text{Null}(A)$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nExpanding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, a basis for $\\text{Null}(A)$ is\n\n$$\nB={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$\n\nsince it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "286a22be-226b-5278-9f0c-13bb759f9a42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433725} {:answer/id #uuid "464a30d1-e864-5afa-9446-1bdfbf96d814" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433729} {:answer/id #uuid "471d07a2-7a00-5445-b039-6e7e52a2ce31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433730} {:answer/id #uuid "742b6147-63b5-5c2d-9b94-e9f574591def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433738} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c8e352-66ef-5b12-8698-69c3539ca0ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433725} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e38ec95-7869-5169-b08c-aa50d0ea1b2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433762}] :question/id #uuid "196e6069-b65f-5278-a39a-6a5091ac25f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-35525" :question/problem "Given that  $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-7{x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{4}\\in R\\}$, find a basis for $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\text{Null}(A)$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-7{x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{4}\\in R.\n$$\n\nExpanding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-7{x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, a basis for $\\text{Null}(A)$ is\n\n$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nsince it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Basis for a Given Null Space"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119818 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119629 :question/id #uuid "a9d2ed82-2ba5-53a6-973d-c859ea5c295f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4821" :question/problem "Find a basis of the null space of the matrix ![](images/35/35651f90fba8141cafc7d513670e9903a4977a2c4bd3a8317ee7be90f4e7c493.svg)" :question/worked-solution "To find a basis of $\\textrm{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{0}$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\textrm{Null}(A).$\n\nThe given matrix is already in reduced row echelon form. So, the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the following system:\n![](images/af/afdd7aba38057c3f4b226c63d103c83d3a76171ae8ae2a900db4c875a9c4e023.svg)\n\nHere, $x_1$ and $x_3$ are basic variables corresponding to the pivot columns ($1$st and $3$rd) and $x_2,x_4$ are free variables corresponding to the non-pivot columns. Therefore, if $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\textrm{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{4}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x_2,x_4\\in\\mathbb{R}.$ This implies that\n\n![](images/4d/4d430991c440bc6e0afad527930566f4c839476f8f1c4f1ee91f2f726d0ece27.svg)\n\nis a basis of $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\textrm{Null}(A).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c70963f-589d-532b-9286-559f68693df7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eae677a-4b0e-5feb-bd73-343cc292bac9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321640} {:answer/id #uuid "77e30b91-e21b-5ee7-95c2-3f3beca8a4fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322088} {:answer/id #uuid "8bb4a8f6-8ebe-5225-8373-b30a575d922c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\,}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322264} {:answer/id #uuid "9dae4a82-2dc7-5a48-a0db-ff103cde4387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322388} {:answer/id #uuid "e55036d9-ba2a-5f7b-a207-1185ce70f8fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322388} :answer-field/id #uuid "47a28f92-97d8-5c8a-8621-fe0f3e5c37b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323303}] :question/id #uuid "6ddc983d-09f4-5bef-b6c1-298b1bde8215" :question/math-academy-id "q-35450" :question/problem "Find a basis of the null space of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nThe given matrix is already in reduced row echelon form. So, the equation $Ax=0$ corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{4} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{4} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}-3{x}_{4} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &={x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-2{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{3} &=3{x}_{4}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHere, ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ are basic variables corresponding to the pivot columns ($1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd) and ${x}_{4}$ is a free variable corresponding to the non-pivot column. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{4} \\\\ -2{x}_{4} \\\\ 3{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{4}\\in R.$ This implies that\n\n$$\nB={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate the $\\text{Null}(A).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120391 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c5749a4-ec1c-5dc8-acde-f00a795944ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = {\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118461} {:answer/id #uuid "adaa4ba3-2626-5837-8660-79b1f98fe821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = {}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118462} {:answer/id #uuid "396fa353-a3a4-5771-86c6-187de2252503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = {\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118463} {:answer/id #uuid "3b22f264-d598-592e-8e3a-882dde3c77f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = {\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118464} {:answer/id #uuid "6f4c3073-ed28-59b9-82f6-103062bd1d7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = {\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118465}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4865cb75-4e12-53d0-a009-4e1bb37d2801" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118460}] :question/id #uuid "ba477a89-340a-5998-8c44-46602bc4a8e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-35503" :question/problem "Find a basis of the the null space of the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247220 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044f3db6-4178-5370-987b-c104d6e9b0ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244348} {:answer/id #uuid "1aaa13d2-6dd5-53d5-9280-da792724674c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244550} {:answer/id #uuid "448279e7-1694-550e-8953-018294384721" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244916} {:answer/id #uuid "c20ed544-fe1d-5293-a762-c0bd05756e63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246043} {:answer/id #uuid "f87a2190-16bd-556f-9a3b-77d7d7179125" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246043} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb61c351-68fb-5878-9057-4a85715b7d71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246968}] :question/id #uuid "dfae24bc-3382-50d4-8245-f369825a9256" :question/math-academy-id "q-111465" :question/problem "Find a basis of the null space of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nThe given matrix is already in reduced row echelon form. So, the equation $Ax=0$ corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{4} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-6{x}_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=-3{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{2} &=6{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHere, ${x}_{1}$ and  ${x}_{2}$ are basic variables corresponding to the pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd), and ${x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are free variable corresponding to the non-pivot columns. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3{x}_{4} \\\\ 6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3},\\,{x}_{4}\\in R.$ This implies that\n\n$$\nB={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate the $\\text{Null}(A).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345015 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02022169-e929-5ff3-a8b0-8a1b9171d655" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342266} {:answer/id #uuid "51ec53d0-c818-53b5-a287-6537ad4e91d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\,}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342918} {:answer/id #uuid "a92d705b-bfb4-5842-869c-238db2751b00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343726} {:answer/id #uuid "b5557627-78bf-5baf-9463-2741bf598f3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343826} {:answer/id #uuid "f53c8a52-60b4-5d4e-a359-1070974a8593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\,}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342918} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf6147b1-ed58-5d20-af7e-b4919fdce625" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344849}] :question/id #uuid "b768fee1-e16c-5c8d-9689-1704de0a0721" :question/math-academy-id "q-75000" :question/problem "Find a basis of the null space of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nThe given matrix is already in row echelon form. So, the equation $Ax=0$ corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the only solution of $Ax=0$ is $x=0.$ So, $\\text{Null}(A)={0},$ which means that the basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ is the empty set, i.e., $B={\\,}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345018 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1857d3fa-4f40-51e1-b806-78d328c14e38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342452} {:answer/id #uuid "43401be9-8f48-5f9b-8777-de583221b7b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342799} {:answer/id #uuid "88af8229-816e-5200-85df-c9e04565d6f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343421} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab4844b-f600-5ed2-9d4f-34aafd08b260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\,}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343444} {:answer/id #uuid "e818b423-1733-5e16-b0b3-7a849790441e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342799} :answer-field/id #uuid "21678c8c-8d2b-5