an (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{1}=\\frac{y-(-2)}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{3}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{1}=\\frac{y+2}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262770 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200e379e-abe3-5da7-b277-56cac4a8cea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{-2}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z-1}{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260149} {:answer/id #uuid "5a7b884a-3b6c-572b-b706-2ae9846ef608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z+1}{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260647} {:answer/id #uuid "65496af8-485a-50cf-864e-c5e46a288620" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{-1}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z+1}{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260752} {:answer/id #uuid "aef45397-9439-5bc0-99b9-59ee9702bae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{2}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z+1}{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261418} {:answer/id #uuid "ce9536f4-1194-5f6c-899f-f4686eb892fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y+5}{1}=\\frac{z+1}{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{-2}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z-1}{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260149} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5241990-a98c-5acd-b933-6502bd5f97ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262420}] :question/id #uuid "e3c58965-d857-5ac7-a5d2-c9236f2e447b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127410" :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the parametric equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3-2t \\\\ y &=-5t \\\\ z &=1-t\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3-2t \\\\ -5t \\\\ 1-t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2t \\\\ -5t \\\\ -t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThis implies that the given line passes through the point $P(3,0,1)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-2,-5,-1⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-2}=\\frac{y-0}{-5}=\\frac{z-1}{-1}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-2}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z-1}{-1}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a065a09-b9ab-5b6e-bdf6-30734806be5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-4}{2}=\\frac{y-5}{5}=\\frac{z-6}{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303103} {:answer/id #uuid "71b1b8f2-924d-508e-b4dd-6f15fae23883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-2}{4}=\\frac{y-5}{5}=\\frac{z+1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303147} {:answer/id #uuid "ed7d22af-1f56-595a-a924-b113e5e11a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{4}=\\frac{y-5}{5}=\\frac{z-1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303946} {:answer/id #uuid "f1869352-a363-5148-8987-9e4b8f26fb16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}=\\frac{y}{5}=\\frac{z}{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303970} {:answer/id #uuid "f5aef388-8ea6-5273-9b99-ac5f1c352d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}=\\frac{y}{5}=\\frac{z}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592